{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 33, :comments ["<b>And that which shall be redeemed from the Levites.</b> Scripture uses the term redemption and not the term purchase, because whatever the Levites sell belongs to Israel and not to them, for they have no portion in the land. It turns out that every buyer from them is as though he is a redeemer, for originally it was his." "<b>And the sale of the house shall go out.</b> What Rashi explained, that this is a separate commandment — that is according to the second interpretation. But according to the first interpretation, it is all one matter." "<b>It is their possession.</b> Masculine form in pausal form, and likewise ״כי אחוזת עולם הוא להם״."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:15:17.422315925Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}